        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>Detail of the antechamber painted vault. The interior arrangement of the tomb is austere and of impressive proportions. The painted composition covers the entire ceiling, and is perhaps unique at the present. It consists of six alternating palmettes and large water-lilies with huge tendrils. One has the impression that this entire colorful ﬂoral complex is ﬂoating on a light blue ground recalling the surface of a lake. A fine marble doorway leads from the antechamber to the main burial chamber.\n</p><p>Macedonian Tomb \n325 – 300 BC\n</p>\nLefkadia, Macedonia, Greece",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
